{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017GwijiK44ZthWWxfTGeEVK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Epic 03 shared vocabulary: the thread-view types (tech design §Interface\n2\t// Definitions). Shared so cli/sdk/tests import one home; the thread-view\n3\t// domain owns the behavior, this module owns only the shapes.\n4\t\n5\texport type Band = \"brief\" | \"detailed\" | \"smooth\";\n6\t\n7\texport interface ViewProfile {\n8\t  name: string;\n9\t  // Target assembled size; whole-entry fills may land under or over (epic\n10\t  // Data Contracts — the bound is a target, not a cap).\n11\t  lowerBound: number;\n12\t  // Band shares of the lower bound; must sum to 100 (AC-2.3).\n13\t  percentages: { full: number; smooth: number; detailed: number; brief: number };\n14\t}\n15\t\n16\t// A user profile entry as configured: a full profile under a new name, or a\n17\t// field-wise override of a built-in (merged by name, AC-2.2). A partial entry\n18\t// whose name matches no built-in has nothing to merge over and is rejected at\n19\t// construction (FC-0.2's unknown-override violation).\n20\texport interface ViewProfileOverride {\n21\t  name: string;\n22\t  lowerBound?: number;\n23\t  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\"percentages\"]>;\n24\t}\n25\t\n26\t// Visibility-boundary budgets (AC-4.x): max > target ≥ floor, all positive.\n27\texport interface VisibilityBudgets {\n28\t  maxTokens: number;\n29\t  targetTokens: number;\n30\t  floorTokens: number;\n31\t}\n32\t\n33\t// ── SDK assembly config (validated at construction, throws on nonsense\n34\t// per the Epic 02 rule) ───────────────────────────────────────────\n35\texport interface SdkViewConfig {\n36\t  profiles?: ViewProfileOverride[]; // merged over built-ins by name\n37\t  visibility?: Partial<VisibilityBudgets>; // defaults: 32000 / 24000 / 8000\n38\t  compactThreshold?: number; // status trigger; default 160000\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\t// Every optional filled by createSdk's central defaults; profiles resolved\n42\t// to complete, validated entries keyed by name.\n43\texport interface ResolvedViewConfig {\n44\t  profiles: Readonly<Record<string, ViewProfile>>;\n45\t  visibility: VisibilityBudgets;\n46\t  compactThreshold: number;\n47\t}\n48\t\n49\t// ── pull / status shapes (the product crossing to the harness) ────\n50\t//\n51\t// The pull's array shape (Story 1, load-bearing for Stories 2–5): band\n52\t// messages first — one `user` message per non-empty band, gradient order\n53\t// brief → detailed → smooth, marker header + snapshot bytes verbatim — then\n54\t// the tail in record order. Tail messages render by the message-kind mapping\n55\t// table (tech design §Tail message rendering), the contract every later\n56\t// story renders into:\n57\t//\n58\t//   | Message kind                       | Role      | Content shape |\n59\t//   |------------------------------------|-----------|---------------|\n60\t//   | user_prompt                        | user      | text verbatim |\n61\t//   | assistant_text                     | assistant | text verbatim |\n62\t//   | assistant_thinking                 | assistant | fenced: `[thinking]\\n<text>\\n[/thinking]` — included (the tail is full fidelity) |\n63\t//   | tool_call                          | assistant | `[tool call · <name>] <compact args>` — deterministic arg rendering, abbreviation rule for oversized args |\n64\t//   | tool_result (ahead of boundary)    | user      | `[tool result · <name>]\\n<full content>` |\n65\t//   | tool_result (at-or-behind boundary)| user      | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (short-form ladder) |\n66\t//   | runtime_note                       | user      | `[runtime note] <text>` |\n67\texport interface ViewMessage {\n68\t  role: \"user\" | \"assistant\";\n69\t  content: string;\n70\t  band?: Band; // band absent ⇒ tail\n71\t}\n72\t\n73\texport interface ViewMeta {\n74\t  compactPoint: number | null; // null ⇒ never compacted (AC-1.3)\n75\t  coveredFrom: number | null;\n76\t  boundaryPosition: number;\n77\t  gapCount: number;\n78\t  degradedCount: number;\n79\t  viewId: string | null;\n80\t  createdAt: string | null;\n81\t}\n82\t\n83\texport interface PullResult {\n84\t  messages: ViewMessage[];\n85\t  meta: ViewMeta;\n86\t}\n87\t\n88\texport interface ViewStatus {\n89\t  tailTokens: number;\n90\t  threshold: number;\n91\t  compactRecommended: boolean;\n92\t  derivation: { pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\n93\t  view: { degraded: number; gaps: number; builtAt: string } | null;\n94\t  visibility: { zoneTokens: number; maxTokens: number };\n95\t}\n96\t\n97\t// ── receipts (AC-2.7, AC-3.x) ─────────────────────────────────────\n98\texport interface CompactReceipt {\n99\t  viewId: string;\n100\t  profile: string | null;\n101\t  config: ViewProfile[\"percentages\"] & { lowerBound: number };\n102\t  bands: Record<Band, { entries: number; tokens: number }>;\n103\t  tailTokens: number;\n104\t  coveredFrom: number;\n105\t  compactPoint: number;\n106\t  degraded: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; usedForm: string }>;\n107\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n108\t  sweep: SweepReceipt | { skipped: true };\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\texport interface SweepReceipt {\n112\t  owners: Array<{\n113\t    owner: \"messages\" | \"turns\";\n114\t    kind: string;\n115\t    ready: number;\n116\t    inFlight: number;\n117\t    requeued: string[]; // subject ids\n118\t    blocked: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n119\t    permanentFailed: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n120\t  }>;\n121\t}\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f","uuid":"cb26cb6f-7e80-4615-83d7-0a89d9e14f68","timestamp":"2026-06-11T15:11:33.486Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts","content":"// Epic 03 shared vocabulary: the thread-view types (tech design §Interface\n// Definitions). Shared so cli/sdk/tests import one home; the thread-view\n// domain owns the behavior, this module owns only the shapes.\n\nexport type Band = \"brief\" | \"detailed\" | \"smooth\";\n\nexport interface ViewProfile {\n  name: string;\n  // Target assembled size; whole-entry fills may land under or over (epic\n  // Data Contracts — the bound is a target, not a cap).\n  lowerBound: number;\n  // Band shares of the lower bound; must sum to 100 (AC-2.3).\n  percentages: { full: number; smooth: number; detailed: number; brief: number };\n}\n\n// A user profile entry as configured: a full profile under a new name, or a\n// field-wise override of a built-in (merged by name, AC-2.2). A partial entry\n// whose name matches no built-in has nothing to merge over and is rejected at\n// construction (FC-0.2's unknown-override violation).\nexport interface ViewProfileOverride {\n  name: string;\n  lowerBound?: number;\n  percentages?: Partial<ViewProfile[\"percentages\"]>;\n}\n\n// Visibility-boundary budgets (AC-4.x): max > target ≥ floor, all positive.\nexport interface VisibilityBudgets {\n  maxTokens: number;\n  targetTokens: number;\n  floorTokens: number;\n}\n\n// ── SDK assembly config (validated at construction, throws on nonsense\n// per the Epic 02 rule) ───────────────────────────────────────────\nexport interface SdkViewConfig {\n  profiles?: ViewProfileOverride[]; // merged over built-ins by name\n  visibility?: Partial<VisibilityBudgets>; // defaults: 32000 / 24000 / 8000\n  compactThreshold?: number; // status trigger; default 160000\n}\n\n// Every optional filled by createSdk's central defaults; profiles resolved\n// to complete, validated entries keyed by name.\nexport interface ResolvedViewConfig {\n  profiles: Readonly<Record<string, ViewProfile>>;\n  visibility: VisibilityBudgets;\n  compactThreshold: number;\n}\n\n// ── pull / status shapes (the product crossing to the harness) ────\n//\n// The pull's array shape (Story 1, load-bearing for Stories 2–5): band\n// messages first — one `user` message per non-empty band, gradient order\n// brief → detailed → smooth, marker header + snapshot bytes verbatim — then\n// the tail in record order. Tail messages render by the message-kind mapping\n// table (tech design §Tail message rendering), the contract every later\n// story renders into:\n//\n//   | Message kind                       | Role      | Content shape |\n//   |------------------------------------|-----------|---------------|\n//   | user_prompt                        | user      | text verbatim |\n//   | assistant_text                     | assistant | text verbatim |\n//   | assistant_thinking                 | assistant | fenced: `[thinking]\\n<text>\\n[/thinking]` — included (the tail is full fidelity) |\n//   | tool_call                          | assistant | `[tool call · <name>] <compact args>` — deterministic arg rendering, abbreviation rule for oversized args |\n//   | tool_result (ahead of boundary)    | user      | `[tool result · <name>]\\n<full content>` |\n//   | tool_result (at-or-behind boundary)| user      | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (short-form ladder) |\n//   | runtime_note                       | user      | `[runtime note] <text>` |\nexport interface ViewMessage {\n  role: \"user\" | \"assistant\";\n  content: string;\n  band?: Band; // band absent ⇒ tail\n}\n\nexport interface ViewMeta {\n  compactPoint: number | null; // null ⇒ never compacted (AC-1.3)\n  coveredFrom: number | null;\n  boundaryPosition: number;\n  gapCount: number;\n  degradedCount: number;\n  viewId: string | null;\n  createdAt: string | null;\n}\n\nexport interface PullResult {\n  messages: ViewMessage[];\n  meta: ViewMeta;\n}\n\nexport interface ViewStatus {\n  tailTokens: number;\n  threshold: number;\n  compactRecommended: boolean;\n  derivation: { pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\n  view: { degraded: number; gaps: number; builtAt: string } | null;\n  visibility: { zoneTokens: number; maxTokens: number };\n}\n\n// ── receipts (AC-2.7, AC-3.x) ─────────────────────────────────────\nexport interface CompactReceipt {\n  viewId: string;\n  profile: string | null;\n  config: ViewProfile[\"percentages\"] & { lowerBound: number };\n  bands: Record<Band, { entries: number; tokens: number }>;\n  tailTokens: number;\n  coveredFrom: number;\n  compactPoint: number;\n  degraded: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; usedForm: string }>;\n  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n  sweep: SweepReceipt | { skipped: true };\n}\n\nexport interface SweepReceipt {\n  owners: Array<{\n    owner: \"messages\" | \"turns\";\n    kind: string;\n    ready: number;\n    inFlight: number;\n    requeued: string[]; // subject ids\n    blocked: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n    permanentFailed: Array<{ subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\n  }>;\n}\n","numLines":122,"startLine":1,"totalLines":122}}}
